/	PDP-12 KALEIDOSCOPE PROGRAM.

/	THIS IS THE ORIGINAL LINC/LINC-8/PDP-12 DISPLAY PROGRAM THAT RUNS ON ALL LINC
/	FAMILY MACHINES.

/	NOTE: THE LOGIC OF THIS PROGRAM HAS BEEN TRANSLATED INTO 100% PDP-8 CODE FOR
/	USE ON SYSTEMS SUCH AS THE LAB-8/E OR AX08; HOWEVER, THE ROOTS OF THIS PROGRAM
/	GO BACK MANY YEARS EARLIER.

/	THIS VERSION WAS UPDATED TO TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THE VR12/VR14 DISPLAY ON THE
/	PDP-12 [WHICH HAS AN ADDITIONAL BIT OF PRECISION IN BOTH DISPLAY AXES].

/	THIS SOURCE CODE WAS CLEANED UP ON 16-JUL-2016 FROM THE ORIGINAL LAP6-DIAL
/	FILE, WHICH WAS PLACED ON THE DEMO LINCTAPE DEC-12-MRZA-U0.  THIS TAPE WAS
/	CREATED WHILE THE PDP-12 WAS STILL IN THE PROTOYPE STAGE AND GENERALLY WAS THE
/	FIRST LINCTAPE USERS WORKED WITH WHEN THEIR NEW PDP-12 SYSTEMS WERE DELIVERED
/	AND SETUP BY FIELD SERVICE.  THE LINCTAPE ITSELF IS A PROVISIONAL EARLY RELEASE
/	OF LAP6-DIAL AND DOES NOT COMPLETELY FUNCTION.  MOST NOTABLY, IT PREDATES THE
/	STARTER SYSTEM LINCTAPES THAT COULD BE USED TO CONFIGURE DIAL-MS.  THIS VERSION
/	OF THE PROGRAM IS GENERALLY CREDITED TO MICHAEL I. GAGE AS OF 12-JUL-1969.  THE
/	CODE FOR THE LESSER DISPLAY OF THE LINC AND LINC-8 LIKELY GOES BACK AT LEAST
/	SIX YEARS EARLIER AS THE CHANGES TO TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THE BETTER DISPLAY ARE
/	MINIMAL.

/	THE TAPE DOCUMENTED ABOVE DOES NOT START UP THE WAY ALL EVENTUAL DIAL TAPES
/	DID, RATHER IT STARTS WITH A WELCOME BALLOON SCREEN AND A PRIMITIVE MENU SYSTEM
/	TO ACCESS MOST OF THE PROGRAMS.  A FEW OF THE PROGRAMS WERE MADE AVAILABLE IN
/	SOURCE AS WELL AS BINARY FORM, MOST NOTABLY MAGSPY, WHICH ALLOWED MANY OF US TO
/	STUDY THE INTERNAL STRUCTURES OF DIAL ITSELF.  [NOTE: THERE WAS AN OBSCURE WAY
/	TO DEFEAT THE MENU SYSTEM TO ACCESS THE UNDERLYING LAP6-DIAL FEATURES, AT LEAST
/	THE ONES THAT ACTUALLY WORKED, NOT MUCH MORE THAN THE DIRECTORY STRUCTURE.]

/	NOTE: MANY OF THE PROGRAMS ON THE DEMO TAPE HAVE SPECIAL FILE NAMES FOR THE
/	BENEFIT OF THE MENU SYSTEM; IT WOULD APPEAR THAT KALEIDOSCOPE IS NOT ONE OF
/	THESE AS IT RETAINS AN ORDINARY AND SELF-EXPLANATORY FILE NAME.  [SINCE IT
/	DERIVES FROM ONE OF THE OLDER LAP SYSTEMS, THE ORIGINAL FILE NAME IS RETAINED
/	AND DOES NOT TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THE EIGHT CHARACTER NAMES ASSOCIATED WITH
/	LAP6-DIAL.]  SOME OF THE OTHER PROGRAMS ON THE DEMO TAPE ARE WELL KNOWN FOR
/	THEIR PRIOR VERSIONS THAT RUN ON THE LINC OR LINC-8.  THE NAMES MAY NOT ALL BE
/	INTUITIVE, BUT THEY ARE AUTHENTIC.  THE READER IS REFERRED TO EARLIER
/	DOCUMENTATION FOR THE LINC/LINC-8 VERSIONS FOR MORE INFORMATION.

/	NOTE: THE PDP-12 KALEIDOSCOPE IS AN EXAMPLE OF EXTREMELY CONFUSING
/	SELF-MODIFYING CODE.  MANY OTHERWISE GOOD 12-BIT MACHINE PROGRAMMERS HAVE GIVEN
/	UP IN TOTAL FRUSTRATION ATTEMPTING TO FULLY UNDERSTAND IT.  TO MAKE MATTERS
/	WORSE, THE ORIGINAL AUTHORS ENGAGED IN A DELIBERATE FORM OF OBFUSCATION BY
/	MAKING THE CODE FAR LESS SYMBOLIC THAN NECESSARY WITHIN REASON.  WHILE THIS
/	ASPECT OF THE CODE COULD HAVE BEEN CLEANED UP, IT HAS NOT CHANGED OTHER THAN
/	SOME ADDED COMMENTS AND APPLYING PROPER SOURCE CODE CONVENTIONS.  THIS ALLOWS
/	THE READER THE "FULL ENJOYMENT" OF ATTEMPTING TO STUDY HOW THE PROGRAM WORKS.
/	PROGRAMMING NOTE:

/	IN PDP-8 PROGRAMMING, THE NOTATION ".-." IS OFTEN USED TO DIFFERENTIATE BETWEEN
/	STORAGE CLEARLY TO BE STORED INTO VERSUS MEMORY THAT MUST CONTAIN THE VALUE
/	0000.  FOR STRICT BINARY COMPATIBILITY WITH THE ORIGINAL PROGRAM, THE VALUE OF
/	ZERO WILL BE ASSEMBLED COMMENTING OUT THE ".-." NOTATION WHERE APPLICABLE.  THE
/	REASON THIS IS NECESSARY IS THAT IN LMODE, THE VALUE GENERATED IS 7777 [WHICH IS
/	THE ONE'S COMPLEMENT RESULT].  SINCE THE INITIAL VALUE IS TRULY UNIMPORTANT, THE
/	".-." NOTATION SHOULD BE RESTORED IN FUTURE EDITS OF THE PROGRAM.

/	CLASSIC PDP-12 KALEIDOSCOPE PROGRAM [KALEID]

/	LAST EDIT ON LAP6-DIAL [PRE-RELEASE]:		07-DEC-1969
/	MICHAEL I. GAGE.

/	LAST EDIT FOR P?S/8 PAL [AND OS/8 PAL12]:	21-JUL-2016
/	CHARLES LASNER P?S NY.

/	ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS AND PROGRAMMING NUANCES.

/	ALL DIAL SOURCE FILES START WITH A *20 TO IDENTIFY THE FILE AS A PROPER SOURCE
/	PROGRAM.  AS SUCH, THE ASSEMBLY MODE IS NOT ALWAYS ESTABLISHED AT THAT POINT.
/	THE DIAL ASSEMBLER IS KNOWN TO ASSUME LMODE IS IN EFFECT; THUS, WHILE SLOPPY,
/	THIS ARCANE "FEATURE" CAN BE ACCOMMODATED BY THE FEW FULLY-COMPATIBLE DUAL-MODE
/	ASSEMBLERS SUCH AS P?S/8 PAL AND CERTAIN [BUT NOT ALL] KNOWN RELEASES OF THE
/	USER PROGRAM PAL12 FOR OS/8.

/	P?S/8 PAL SUPPORTS DIAL-COMPATIBLE LMODE PROGRAMMING AS AN OPTION, WHICH CAN BE
/	STARTED EITHER IN PMODE BY DEFAULT OR LMODE BY DEFAULT BY USING THE '/8' OR
/	'/9' COMMAND-LINE SWITCHES RESPECTIVELY.  ADDITIONALLY, IT IS RECOMMENDED THE
/	'/Q' AND '/O' COMMAND-LINE SWITCHES NOT BE USED; THIS DISABLES THE LITERAL AND
/	LINK-GENERATING FEATURES OF P?S/8 PAL WHICH TAKE UP MEMORY [AND AREN'T NEEDED
/	FOR THIS ASSEMBLY].  THIS WILL GENERALLY ALLOW PROPER ASSEMBLY ON A 4K SYSTEM.
/	[NOTE: P?S/8 PAL TAKES ADVANTAGE OF ANY ADDITIONAL MEMORY UP TO AS MUCH AS 20K.
/	IF AVAILABLE MEMORY IS LARGER THAN THE MINIMUM REQUIREMENT, THESE INSTRUCTIONS
/	CAN BE IGNORED, OTHER THAN THE REQUIREMENT TO ENABLE THE '/9' COMMMAND-LINE
/	SWITCH.]  ALL OTHER COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES CAN BE SET IN P?S/8 PAL THAT
/	WOULD APPLY FOR ANY FORM OF PROGRAM ASSEMBLY LISTING AND/OR BINARY OUTPUT FILE
/	CREATION.  THE USER IS REFERRED TO THE P?S/8 PAL COMMAND GUIDE AVAILABLE FROM
/	CHARLES LASNER FOR FURTHER DOCUMENTATION OF P?S/8 PAL.

/	NOTE: THIS SOURCE FILE SHOULD ALSO ASSEMBLE PROPERLY WITH APPROPRIATE VERSIONS
/	OF OS/8 PAL12; HOWEVER, PAL12 IS NOT A DEC PRODUCT.  PAL12 WAS WRITTEN BY
/	SEVERAL GROUPS OF OS/8 USERS AS A MODIFICATION OF THEN-CURRENT PAL8; NOT ALL
/	RELEASES OF PAL12 ACTUALLY FUNCTION PROPERLY [FOR A VARIETY OF REASONS].  AT THE
/	TIME OF THIS WRITING, NO FULLY COMPATIBLE RELEASES OF PAL12 HAVE BEEN LOCATED.
/	THIS DOCUMENTATION WILL BE UPDATED WHEN THE SPECIFIC REQUIREMENTS OF A WORKING
/	PAL12 CAN BE DETERMINED.
/	LINC-MODE SEGMENT ADDRESSING CONSIDERATIONS.

/	ALL LINC ADDRESSES ARE RELATIVE TO THE CURRENT MEMORY SEGMENT OF 1K 12-BIT
/	WORDS.  ORIGINS SET IN LMODE LESS THAN 2000 WILL BECOME THE 12-BIT ADDRESS OF
/	THE CURRENT SEGMENT IN EFFECT; HOWEVER, THIS VALUE CAN BE OVERRIDEN FOR MOST
/	OTHER ADDRESS RANGES BY USING LARGER VALUES THAT SET ONE OR BOTH HIGH-ORDER
/	BITS OF THE ABSOLUTE ADDRESS.  WHILE THIS IS CLEARLY AN ASYMMETRICAL SITUATION,
/	THIS IS THE WAY ALL COMPATIBLE ASSEMBLERS ACTUALLY WORK; FURTHER, CERTAIN
/	ASSEMBLERS MAY NOT MAKE THIS CLEAR UNLESS ASSEMBLING IN PMODE.  [NOTE: THIS IS
/	NOT A PROBLEM IN P?S/8 PAL AS THE ACTUAL 12-BIT ADDRESS IS ALWAYS DISPLAYED IN
/	THE ASSEMBLY LISTING.]  THE DEFAULT VALUE IS SEGMENT 02; AS SUCH, THE *20
/	OPENING STATEMENT REFERS TO LOCATION 04020.  THIS IS ALSO THE DEFAULT STARTING
/	ADDRESS ON THE PDP-12 FRONT PANEL WHEN THE "START 20" KEY IS PRESSED ASSUMING
/	THE SEGMENT REGISTERS ARE SET TO THEIR POWER-ON DEFAULTS.  [THIS MEANS THE
/	INSTRUCTION SEGMENT IS 04000-05777 AND THE DATA SEGMENT IS 06000-07777.  ON THE
/	LINC-8 THESE VALUES ARE OFTEN DIFFERENT AND SET BY THE OPERATING SYSTEM IN USE.
/	ON THE LINC, THERE IS ONLY ONE INSTRUCTION SEGMENT AND ONE DATA SEGMENT AS THE
/	LINC IS LIMITED TO 2K OF MEMORY AND LACKS SEGMENT CHANGE REGISTERS.]

/	PMODE STARTING ON OPERATING SYSTEMS WITH TYPICAL PDP-8 MEMORY RESTRICTIONS.

/	MANY PROGRAMS THAT RUN FROM LAP6-DIAL OR DIAL-MS DEPEND ON MEMORY CONVENTIONS
/	THAT DIFFER GREATLY FROM PDP-8 STANDARDS.  NOTE: PROGRAMS WRITTEN FOR DIAL
/	OFTEN INCLUDE HARD-WIRED LINCTAPE INSTRUCTIONS KNOWN TO START A DIAL LINCTAPE.
/	AS SUCH, THERE ARE NO RESTRICTIONS TO THE CONTENTS OF FIELD 0 ASSUMING THIS
/	NON-FORMAL EXIT MECHANISM IS USED.  THIS IS BASED ON LONG-STANDING CONVENTIONS
/	FOR THE LINC AND LINC-8; ALL OF THESE SYSTEMS RUN EXCLUSIVELY ON LINCTAPES.  IF
/	DIAL-MS IS THE ACTUAL OPERATING ENVIRONMENT, THE SAME LINCTAPE OPERATION WILL
/	BOOT THAT SYSTEM AS WILL BECAUSE THE MORE GENERAL BOOTUP CONVENTION IS USED THAT
/	CAN DETECT THE DIAL-MS RESIDENT SECTION IN EXTENDED MEMORY.

/	BY ADDING IN A PMODE SECTION THAT LOADS INTO MEMORY EXTERNAL TO THE APPLICATION
/	PROGRAMMING, IT IS POSSIBLE TO START AT 00200 WHICH IS THE DEFAULT PDP-8
/	STARTING ADDRESS.  NOTE: THE ONLY RESTRICTION IS THE APPLICATION NOT LOAD INTO
/	07600-07777.  VIRTUALLY ALL APPLICATION PROGRAMS OF THIS TYPE LOAD INTO 04020
/	AND FOLLOWING, AS THIS IS THE DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS ON ALL LINC-BASED
/	PROGRAMS; VIRTUALLY ALL OF THEM ARE WRITTEN FOR COMPATIBILITY WITH THE 2K
/	ORIGINAL LINC.  FORTUNATELY, MOST OF THESE PROGRAMS DO NOT EXTENDED INTO 07600
/	AND FOLLOWING.  FOR THE EXCEPTION CASES, IT MAY BE NECESSARY TO MAKE SIGNIFICANT
/	CHANGES TO THE SOURCE CODE TO AT LEAST BE COMPATIBLE WITH THIS CONVENTION DURING
/	THE LOADING PROCESS.  AFTER THE PROGRAM IS STARTED, IT WILL BE NECESSARY TO
/	MANUALLY REBOOT THE OPERATING SYSTEM.

/	FOR MORE INFORMATION, CONSULT THE "PSTART" PROGRAM AVAILABLE SEPARATELY.
*20					/THIS IS HOW THE DIAL FILE STARTS; THE *20 IS
					/USED TO INDICATE THE FILE IS ACTUALLY A VALID
					/ASSEMBLER SOURCE FILE.  THIS IS NOT DISPLAYED
					/IN THE DIAL FILE EDITOR AND CANNOT BE REMOVED.

/	BINARY COMPATIBILITY ISSUES.

/	NOTE: IF STRICT BINARY COMPATIBILITY WITH BINARY PAPER-TAPE VERSIONS OF ANY OF
/	THE PDP-12 APPLICATIONS [SUCH AS KALEID] IS UNNECESSARY, THE "*20" ABOVE CAN BE
/	REMOVED OR COMMENTED OUT; DOING SO CHANGES NOTHING WITH RESPECT TO PROGRAM
/	FUNCTION.  [THIS SOURCE PROGRAM WAS WRITTEN FOR 100% COMPATIBILITY WITH
/	EXISTING BIN FORMAT BINARY PAPER-TAPE RELEASES.]

/	KALEID [SOMETIMES ERRONEOUSLY KNOWN AS KALIED].

/	PDP-12 VERSION OF KALEIDOSCOPE.

/	PROGRAM CONTROLS.

/	THE SCOPE PATTERN CHANGES BY SAM 7 AND SAM 10.  SAM 7 IS CONTROLLED BY A
/	FRONT-PANEL POTENTIOMETER.  SAM 10 REQUIRES AN EXTERNAL INPUT ON A-D CHANNEL 10
/	TO ALLOW AN ADDITIONAL LEVEL OF REMOTE CONTROL OF DISPLAY RANDOMNESS.  [NOTE: IT
/	MAY BE NECESSARY TO CONSTRUCT A FRONT-END PREAMPLIFIER DEPENDING ON THE NATURE
/	OF THE EXTERNAL DEVICE.]

/	NOTE: IF A VERSION OF THE "PSTART" PROGRAM IS USED TO START THIS PROGRAM,
/	ADDITIONAL CONSIDERATIONS COULD APPLY.

/	CREATED FOR THE PDP-12 [AS OPPOSED TO THE LINC AND LINC-8 VERSIONS] BY:
/	MICHAEL I GAGE: 07-DEC-1969

	PMODE				/ENSURE 12-BIT ADDRESS IS KNOWN [ONLY NEEDED BY
					/A FEW ASSEMBLERS].

	*4020				/THE USUAL STARTING ADDRESS FOR LMODE PROGRAMS.

	LMODE				/GOTO L... MODE.  [NOTE: MANY PDP-8 PROGRAMMERS
					/REFER TO PMODE AS "GOODY" MODE. THIS IS
					/BECAUSE OF THEIR GENERAL DISDAIN FOR LINC MODE
					/ADDRESSING RULES.]

/	THE PROGRAM STARTS HERE.

A,	LDA I;	0000			/LOAD WHAT'S [CURRENTLY] IN LOCATION A+1 TO AC.
	SCR	0			/SCALE RIGHT [BEWARE OF BIT CHANGES!]
	COM				/INVERT THE AC.
	ADM;	.+7			/THIS MAY NOT DO WHAT YOU THINK!
	BCL I;	4000			/WANT UNSIGNED VALUE FOR THE DISPLAY.
	STC	1			/SETUP ONE DISPLAY COORDINATE.
	ADD	.+12			/GET THE OTHER DISPLAY COORDINATE.
	DIS	1			/DISPLAY A POINT.
	LDA I;	1777
	SCR	0			/MORE BIT CHANGES.
	ADM;	.-16			/DID YOU SEE WHAT CHANGED?
	ADA I;	-6377
	STA I;	0/.-.
	DIS	1			/DISPLAY A POINT.
	SAM	7			/GET KNOB 7 VALUE.
	STC	.+3
	SAM	10			/GET EXTERNAL VALUE ON CHANNEL 10.
	ADA I;	SAM	7		/[NOT REALLY WHAT IT SAYS.]
	APO				/CHECK IF A VALID COMPOSITE VALUE.
	JMP	A			/ELSE IGNORE IT.
	BCL I;	7774
	AZE I				/SKIP IF NON-ZERO.
	JMP	A			/ELSE IGNORE IT.
	ADA I;	SCR	0		/WATCH OUT FOR BIT CHANGES!
	STA;	A+2
	STC	A+15
	JMP	A			/GO DO IT AGAIN.

	$				/THAT'S ALL FOLK!
